  "effectiveTerms": "GPL-3.0-or-later for the engine, SurgeScript's runtime (Apache-2.0, compatible) and this core's integration; each game file under its own licence, listed with its author",
  "commercialUse": "allowed (the engine is GPL-3.0; the game files are CC-BY, CC-BY-SA, CC0, MIT, Apache-2.0, OFL-1.1 and Giftware: each asks that its author is credited, and the CC-BY-SA files that a changed copy of them is shared on the same terms)",
  "note": "The built core is the Open Surge Engine compiled with the patches in patches/ (a modified copy of its source: the corresponding source is this repository at the commit the package names, and the commits its submodules pin), on Allegro 5 with drivers of this core's own in place of a window system, SurgeScript, PhysicsFS, FreeType, libpng, zlib, libogg and libvorbis, and with Mesa's softpipe OpenGL. The package carries Surge the Rabbit's game files (the engine's own sample game: its pictures, sound effects, music, fonts, levels and scripts) as one zip inside the program. Each is credited in the engine's credits screen and in src/misc/copyright_data.csv (the last licence text of the package), which names the author and the licence of every file; the licence texts are in licenses/. The CC-BY-SA files (ten music tracks, and two pictures) are shipped unchanged, beside the program and not in it: their share-alike terms are theirs only.",
